WEBVTT

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.760
There.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.750
Hey, mister.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.140
Could you take care of these?

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.830
There's a bicycle in the 
black one, so be careful.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.460
<b>The Minami Kamakura Bicycle
Club is at your shop, Korone</b>

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.970
I finished packing everything up,
little girl.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.540
You sure do have a lot of stuff.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.210
Thanks, mister.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.480
By the way, I'm an adult.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:38.890
What?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.790
Now, then...

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.350
The bicycle club, huh?

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.470
Let's see what they're like.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:19.320
<b>#5  Choosing a Bicycle is Hard?</b>

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.320
<b>Principal's Office</b>

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.070
What do you mean, the bicycle 
club is being disbanded?

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.040
I'm not finished.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.660
I'm always telling you to listen.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.040
I've only given you provisional 
permission to form a club.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.090
In order to be acknowledged as an
official club, you need to produce results.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.470
Uh, results?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.970
What exactly does that mean?

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.040
You'll have to come up with 
something on your own.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.730
I expect to see something 
within three months.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.870
Th-Three months?

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.860
That's not enough time!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.760
Yeah, and we're beginners.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.610
Yeah.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.790
It's the rules.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:03.160
Without results, you'll be 
considered a circle instead,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.980
and the bicycle club will be disbanded.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.420
We need to produce results,
but I don't know what we should do.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.750
It probably won't be enough 
to just ride around the area.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:21.020
Or cycling to various places 
and enjoying the local cuisine.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.570
Yeah.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.800
This is the kind of thing we 
should discuss with Shiki-sensei.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.760
Come to think of it, where is she?

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.150
She's still not here?

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:33.350
She said she would come, but...

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:38.010
These club activity forms never end!

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.510
There's insurance, expenses, and schedules!

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.360
What else do I need?

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.970
In any case, we need to buy bicycles first.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.830
We can't produce results without those.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:52.790
Yeah, but the store's still not open!

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.540
What's going on, Tsuru-san?

00:03:55.540 --> 00:04:00.840
The manager came back yesterday 
and was supposed to open up today.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.730
It can't be helped.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.870
We'll have to come back tomorrow.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:06.850
Yeah.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.570
I hope the manager comes back soon.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:12.970
Oh? You wanted to see me?

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:13.640
What?

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.740
Down here.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:18.110
What?

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.740
She's so cute!

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.010
She even has cat ears.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.340
And a tail.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.570
Are they real?

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.250
H-Hey, stop that!

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.500
Manager, you're back.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.680
What? Manager?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.680
Hey.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.460
She's just a child.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.600
A ch-child? No!

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.300
I'm an adult! A full-grown adult!

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.820
I'm the manager of Cycle Flat, Hooji Korone.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.010
What?

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:53.890
I can't believe the manager 
is a cute little girl.

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:56.480
I told you, I'm an adult.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.600
Who are you girls?

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.360
You look like Minami Kamakura High students.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:07.570
Are you the bicycle club 
Nagisa told me about?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.530
Thank you.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:12.790
I see.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:17.030
So you formed a bicycle club, but now 
it's in danger of being disbanded.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.210
Yes.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.930
I heard you came to check out 
the bikes a bunch of times.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.050
Sorry I was closed for so long.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.800
Manager, I was worried about you.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.810
Sorry, sorry. I was delayed 
by the typhoon in Taiwan.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.020
I had to stay an extra day.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.770
Sorry I couldn't call either.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.020
What is that?

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.460
Amazing, isn't it?

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.610
I bought it at the electronics 
district over there.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.820
Um, what about the trade show?

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.140
Of course I went.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:50.540
Since Taiwan's one of the world's 
leading bicycle producers,

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.790
I got to see all kinds of bikes.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:57.530
What? Taiwan makes that many bikes?

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.330
Yeah, they produce a lot of parts, too.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:05.640
Those bikes you're riding probably 
use Taiwanese parts, too.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.170
Really?

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.510
I didn't know that.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:14.600
Well, I visited places other than the 
trade show and the electronics district, too.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.290
Look at this. It's only 
spring, but I got a tan.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.820
Jeez, again?

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.000
By the way, where's Nagisa?

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.320
She's out getting her license.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.140
Again? What is it this time?

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.110
Special large size vehicles.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.430
Special large?

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:34.080
What does she want to be?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.090
I'm a baker.

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.210
It should be a baker.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.370
Well, whatever.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.250
Right now these girls need bikes.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:46.130
I'll open up the shop for you.
Come around the front.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.570
This is my shop, Cycle Flat.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:08.230
There are so many bicycles.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:11.920
It feels so different from 
the bike shop in town.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.320
There's quite an assortment.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:18.290
Yeah. She's got road racers 
and hybrid bikes, too.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:21.430
Which one's the fastest?

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.200
This is kind of amazing.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:26.210
Just seeing all these bikes 
lined up is exciting.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.750
Yeah, seriously.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:31.050
Come to think of it, 
when I was in grade school...

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:39.680
Among all the bikes, there was 
a pink one that stood out to me.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.440
I remember I wanted it so badly,
my parents bought it for me.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:49.900
I felt like I could go anywhere and 
rode all around the neighborhood.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:55.060
I probably enjoyed how 
my world was expanding.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.910
I think I know what you mean.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.070
I hope I experience that, too.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.600
Hey, you girls have a second?

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:11.050
There's some stuff you need 
to know before buying a bike.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.730
Choosing your partner is 
an important decision.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.090
Listen closely.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.880
Thank you.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:29.270
First, bikes are broadly divided 
into sports and utility types.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:37.620
Sports bikes are road racers, hybrid bikes,
BMX bikes, and mountain bikes.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:42.120
Utility bikes are your standard bikes,
like mommy bikes.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:45.620
Wow, there are all kinds.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.550
I don't care about that.

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:49.450
Just give me your fastest and easiest bike.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:50.590
Idiot!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:50.590
Ow!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.600
I'm not finished talking.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:58.050
You girls have to produce results 
within three months, right?

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.470
Even though you're mostly beginners.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:00.690
Yeah.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:02.030
There's no way.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:03.140
Yeah.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:07.270
Yes. Given your situation,
I'll start with the answer.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:12.910
What you girls need are road racers.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.130
I've ridden one before.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:19.580
Just for a little bit, though.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:20.550
Really?

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:23.660
But why road racers?

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:28.380
Because it's easiest to make 
improvements in distance and speed

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.630
in a short amount of time.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.800
And nothing's better at 
that than road racers.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:37.880
With a road bike, you can 
participate in races,

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:41.600
ride to work or school, or even go pottering.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:45.310
Since they're built for paved roads,
they're great for riding long distances, too.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:50.770
Japan has a lot of paved roads, so you'll 
be able to go all over the place.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:54.770
But when I rode one the other day,
it hurt my butt really bad.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:57.770
I don't think I'd be able 
to ride one for very long.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.450
Yeah, everyone says that at first.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.390
What about you, Natsumi?

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:03.950
Does it not hurt your butt?

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.040
It did at first.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.410
I knew it.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:11.520
I see. Natsumi-chan's butt split in two, too.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.210
Eventually, it'll split into four.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:15.460
Is it only hard on your butt?

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:20.470
I had trouble getting used to the handles.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:24.890
Since the tires are so narrow, 
I was scared of curbs and grates.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.870
And then there's the forward-leaning posture.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:30.010
It hurt my neck and hips.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:31.960
That's a lot of challenges.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.730
Road racers seem like a lot of work.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:37.020
But the fun outweighs the negatives.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.860
You move so far just by 
turning the pedals a little.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.680
You feel like you're one with your bike.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:45.200
Once you start riding, you keep going faster.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.900
Sometimes before I even realize it, 
I've gone really far.

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:54.960
With road racers, you can go to places so
far away, you'd usually go by car or train.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:11:00.080
Yeah. Some guys like taking their road 
racers to highly-rated ramen shops

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.920
and bakeries located far away.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.350
We get a lot of customers 
like that at our shop.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.000
I have a question.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.730
Is the road racer the best all-purpose bike?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:18.190
An all-purpose bike, huh? That would be...

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.470
That would be...

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:21.730
There isn't one.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.780
There's no such thing as an all-purpose bike.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.000
What?

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:28.440
If you have baggage, you want a mommy bike.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.610
If you want to go fast, 
you want a road racer.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:34.690
If you want to ride medium distances or 
through cities, you want a hybrid bike.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.990
If you want to carry your 
bike to your destination

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.800
to ride once you get there, 
you want a small wheel bike.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:44.800
In other words, modern bicycles 
are specialized for their uses.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:50.090
People have individuality, too,
so you don't have all-purpose people.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:53.940
Bikes may look similar,
but they have individuality, too.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:12:00.440
And matching that individuality to the rider 
is an important part of choosing a bike.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:04.340
I like how childlike you are, manager.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:06.270
Who are you calling childlike?

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.890
I told you, I'm an adult!

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:10.460
I mean on the inside.

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:12.830
I'm an adult on the inside, too!

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:16.710
Real bikes are expensive, though.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.470
It depends on the material of the frame.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:23.180
They run from sixty thousand yen
to over a million yen.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:25.520
A million yen?

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:29.340
Tomo-chan, if we had a million yen, 
we could travel across the world!

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.640
Y-Yeah.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:37.670
The lighter a bike is, the easier it is to 
ride up hills and the farther you can go.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:40.820
That's why people prefer 
materials like carbon.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:45.200
<b>Light</b>

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.820
But they get more and more expensive.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:47.910
In other words, light equals expensive.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.910
<b>Light = Expensive</b>

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:51.040
I had no idea.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.570
We should discuss your budget, 
but since I've got test bikes,

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:02.300
I'll make an exception for you today.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.380
I'll let you ride everything here.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.260
Let me know if you're 
interested in any of them.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.970
I don't know which one to choose.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.320
Yeah.

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.430
Choose whatever you like.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:16.020
It can be based on intuition or color.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:20.850
Okay, let's find our partners.

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:25.490
Yeah. With this many bikes,
I'm sure we'll each find one we like.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.040
You're not going to ride one?

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:48.430
I already have a road bike.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:51.430
It doesn't matter. Ride whatever you want.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.390
Thank you.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.190
Okay, everyone's ready.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:08.860
Go test them out on flats and hills.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.740
We're off.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.800
Shopkeeper, I like this one.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:33.710
I'll take this Pi... whatever.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:34.950
It's "Pinarello."

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.030
I'd like this Liv, please.

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:41.120
What about you, Hiromi?

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.420
Well...

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:43.500
Is something wrong?

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.920
I'm not sure.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:51.800
They were all fun and easy to ride, 
but none of them stood out to me.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:52.930
I see.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.960
I'm going to spend more time looking.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.010
Is that okay?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.480
Yeah, take your time.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.610
This one...

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.300
Are you interested in that one?

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:41.810
Um, can I try riding this one?

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.560
Yeah, of course.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.640
It's just the right size for you, too.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:48.450
Okay, go take her for a spin.

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.270
Okay.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:24.850
<i>This one's really fun.</i>

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:28.060
<i>I'm not sure what's 
different about it, but...</i>

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:32.730
How'd it go?

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.090
This one was really easy to ride.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.950
I'd like this one.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.870
Hiromi, you finally found one?

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:41.130
Yeah.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:46.460
Um, about the price...

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:52.380
It's... It's... It's...

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:55.260
It's expensive!

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:59.800
It's a pretty good price for 
the performance, though.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.430
Tomo-chan, what about you?

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:07.410
Well, if I help around my family's shop a 
little more, I think I can afford it.

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:08.480
Really?

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:11.690
I won't have much spending 
money left, though.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:16.190
But since I'll be riding it a lot with 
our club, I want to get one I like.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.370
Yeah. Yeah, you're right.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:23.280
I like this one, but...

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:33.110
I finally finished filling out forms.

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:35.340
Good work, Shiki-sensei.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.230
H-Hello, ma'am.

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:40.850
Has the club decided what it's doing yet?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:45.850
I was thinking we could discuss how we 
can produce results as a club after this.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:49.810
If you haven't settled on anything yet,
then how about this?

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.830
What?

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.990
<b>Sold</b>

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.990
<b>Sold</b>

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.990
Lucky.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.820
Don't let it get you down.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:01.970
You'll find one you like eventually.

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:06.390
You'll have more fun because 
it's the bike you wanted.

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.580
You'll work harder because 
it's the one you chose.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:11.420
You'll trust your bike because 
it's the one you like.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:15.370
That's the best kind of 
bike a person can ride.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:20.090
The bike I like is the best bike for me?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.260
Don't rush. Take your time finding one.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.440
Yeah, thanks.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:29.180
But we have to produce results.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.660
We can't take too long.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:33.900
Oh, right.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.310
Girls!

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:37.240
It's Shiki-sensei.

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:40.360
She finally came.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.590
She seems to be in a hurry.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:43.530
I wonder what's up.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:45.530
Thanks for waiting.

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:50.000
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.980
I found just the right thing.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:52.910
What?

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:56.170
What do you think? Isn't it perfect 
for producing results?

00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:59.420
What is this?

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:03.580
Night Criterium?

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:40.100
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

