00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:59.110
<i>Cycling is fun, but sometimes you 
run into unexpected problems...</i>

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:01.880
"Something's not right."

00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:05.470
"It's flat! This sucks."

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:10.430
"What? But there aren't any 
bike shops around here."

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:13.380
"What should I do?"

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:21.560
<b>Dealing With Accidents 1: Flat Tires</b>

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:18.270
<i>This time we'll learn techniques 
for repairing a flat tire</i>

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:20.300
<i>that even beginners can use.</i>

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:24.400
Is it possible for us to repair 
a flat tire by ourselves?

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:24.940
Yes.

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:29.530
<b>Y's Road Ochanomizu
Manager Yamada Yunosuke-san</b>

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:31.710
The wheels can be removed, so it's a 
useful maintenance technique to learn.

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:32.870
So we can do it ourselves.

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:32.870
Wow.

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:34.060
Really?

00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:34.690
First, I'll remove the tire.

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:35.540
Okay.

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:38.170
There's the valve that's used to add air...

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:40.920
But we'll start working on the opposite side.

00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:43.420
<b>Begin removing the tire from the side opposite of the valve</b>

00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:42.210
It's easier to remove this way.

00:22:42.690 --> 00:22:43.420
I see.

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:45.090
<b>Tire Lever</b>

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:45.090
There's a lip on one end of these.

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:49.680
Hook it into the tire and fold it 
down using the principle of leverage.

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:49.680
Wow.

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:50.370
It folded down.

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:51.760
That's how this tool works.

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:58.940
<b>Remove the tube from the inside and swap it out</b>

00:22:52.630 --> 00:22:56.670
<i>Once you've removed the tire and 
swapped out the tube on the inside,</i>

00:22:56.670 --> 00:22:58.270
<i>you're finished, but...</i>

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:03.270
If possible, you should try to determine 
what caused the flat tire.

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:04.730
<b>Remove the cause of the puncture from the tire</b>

00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:02.540
Okay.

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:04.730
First, we establish a rule.

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:07.150
Align the tire's logo with the valve.

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:10.570
<b>Align the tire's logo sticker with the valve on the tube</b>

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.360
Think of this section as one piece.

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:12.460
Next, I'll inflate the tire.

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:19.740
If you keep the valve and logo 
together, if the hole's here,

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:23.960
then you should be able to find the cause 
if you search this section of the tire.

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:27.660
If there's something wrong with this part, 
then you know it's right here.

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:27.660
That's right.

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:30.210
In order to determine the 
cause of the problem,

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:34.930
<b>Next Time
Dealing With Accidents 2</b>

00:23:30.210 --> 00:23:33.490
it's important to establish your own rule.

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:34.930
It's a good idea to establish 
a rule for yourself.

